    "['set system login user [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'username client002 privilege 15 secret xyz456', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'username client002 privilege 15 secret xyz456', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco IOS configuration for the specified Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\nusername client002 privilege 15 secret xyz456\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- `username client002` creates the user account (equivalent to Juniper\\'s `set system login user client002`)\\n- `privilege 15` sets the privilege level to maximum (equivalent to Juniper\\'s `operator` class)\\n- `secret xyz456` sets the encrypted password (Cisco automatically encrypts cleartext passwords when using `secret`)\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS:\\n1. Privilege level 15 is roughly equivalent to Juniper\\'s \"operator\" class (full operational privileges)\\n2. The dollar sign prefix isn\\'t used in Cisco for password specification - the router will automatically encrypt the password when using the `secret` keyword\\n3. Cisco doesn\\'t have direct equivalents for all Juniper user classes, so privilege levels are used instead', 'trans_template': 'username client002 privilege 15 secret xyz456'}]]": 1,
